# TimeGrid — AI Setup Instructions

When the user says `/setup`, run all the steps below automatically without asking questions. Install any missing prerequisites, then set up and start the project. Do not stop to ask for confirmation between steps.

## /setup Command

Execute these steps in order. If a step fails, try to fix it (install the missing tool, switch versions, etc.) and retry before moving on.

### Step 1: Check and install prerequisites

```bash
# Check PHP version — need 8.2+
php -v

# If PHP is missing or below 8.2, install it:
# macOS: brew install php
# Ubuntu: sudo apt install php8.3 php8.3-cli php8.3-mbstring php8.3-xml php8.3-curl php8.3-sqlite3

# Check Composer — install if missing
composer --version || (curl -sS https://getcomposer.org/installer | php && sudo mv composer.phar /usr/local/bin/composer)

# Check Node.js — need 18+
node -v

# If Node is missing or below 18:
# macOS: brew install node
# Ubuntu: curl -fsSL https://deb.nodesource.com/setup_20.x | sudo -E bash - && sudo apt install -y nodejs
```

### Step 2: Install dependencies

```bash
cd modern
composer install --no-interaction
npm install
```

### Step 3: Environment setup

```bash
cd modern
cp .env.example .env
php artisan key:generate
```

### Step 4: Database setup (SQLite — zero config)

```bash
cd modern
touch database/database.sqlite
php artisan migrate --force
```

### Step 5: Seed demo data

```bash
cd modern
php artisan db:seed --class=DemoSeeder
```

### Step 6: Build frontend

```bash
cd modern
npm run build
```

### Step 7: Start the server

```bash
cd modern
php artisan serve
```

### Step 8: Confirm success

After the server starts, tell the user:

- App is running at http://localhost:8000
- Demo logins:
  - Owner: owner@timegrid.io / password
  - Customer: customer@timegrid.io / password
  - Root: root@timegrid.io / password

---

## /dev Command

When the user says `/dev`, start both the Laravel server and Vite dev server for hot-reload:

```bash
cd modern
php artisan serve &
npm run dev
```

---

## Project Notes

- The project uses SQLite by default — no MySQL/database server setup needed
- The `.env.example` is pre-configured for SQLite with sensible defaults
- Frontend: React 19 + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS via Inertia.js
- Backend: Laravel 11 with Breeze authentication
- All app code lives in the `modern/` directory
